n exposure to BPs, neither for other industrial chemicals with diverse sources in municipal wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(172,'暴露/生活方式标志物','环境暴露标志物','内分泌干扰物/双酚类','双酚AF',NULL,'其他','双酚AF','1478-61-1','分子量336.2 g/mol；水溶性22 mg/L(25°C)；LogKow 3.975；饱和蒸气压3.38E-5 mm Hg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bisphenol analogues; Biomonitoring; Wastewater-based epidemiology; South China','10.1016/j.envres.2021.112398','Bisphenol analogues (BPs) are heavily used and negatively affect the health of human beings, however, there is little knowledge regarding human exposure to BPs other than BPA. This study aims to assess human exposure to BPs through investigating pooled urine and wastewater samples. Twenty-four pooled urine samples were prepared from 960 specimens. Wastewater samples were collected from six major wastewater treatment plants in Guangzhou, South of China. BPA, BPS, and BPAF were widely detected in urine samples. Most BPs were detected in wastewater samples, of which BPA and BPS were predominant BPs. Urinary BPA, BPS, and BPAF accounted for less than 5% per capital mass loads in wastewater, suggesting that much of the BPA, BPS, and BPAF in municipal wastewater originate non-human excretion. Hence, the wastewater-based epidemiology approach based on parent compounds is not available for assessing human exposure to BPs, neither for other industrial chemicals with diverse sources in municipal wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(173,'药物类','抗生素','抗结核药物','乙胺丁醇','结核病治疗（论文研究语境）','处方药','乙胺丁醇','74-55-5','标准品为Ethambutol hydrochloride；分子量277.2 g/mol；LogP -0.059',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tuberculosis drugs; wastewater analysis; Chromatography; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e30720','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is a robust tool for disease surveillance and monitoring of pharmaceutical consumption. However, monitoring tuberculosis (TB) drug consumption faces challenges due to limited data availability. This study aimed to optimise methods for detecting TB drugs in treated and untreated wastewater from four African countries: South Africa, Nigeria, Kenya, and Cameroon. The limit of detection and limit of quantification varied among the target drugs and sites. Application of the optimised method for drug detection and quantification in both treated and untreated wastewater unveiled varied results, with ethambutol consistently most detected and pyrazinamide and isoniazid least detected.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(174,'药物类','抗生素','抗结核药物','吡嗪酰胺','结核病治疗（论文研究语境）','处方药','吡嗪酰胺','98-96-4','分子量123.1 g/mol；LogP -0.6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tuberculosis drugs; wastewater analysis; Chromatography; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e30720','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is a robust tool for disease surveillance and monitoring of pharmaceutical consumption. However, monitoring tuberculosis (TB) drug consumption faces challenges due to limited data availability. This study aimed to optimise methods for detecting TB drugs in treated and untreated wastewater from four African countries: South Africa, Nigeria, Kenya, and Cameroon. The limit of detection and limit of quantification varied among the target drugs and sites. Application of the optimised method for drug detection and quantification in both treated and untreated wastewater unveiled varied results, with ethambutol consistently most detected and pyrazinamide and isoniazid least detected.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(175,'药物类','抗生素','抗结核药物','异烟肼','结核病治疗（论文研究语境）','处方药','异烟肼','54-85-3','分子量137.1 g/mol；LogP -0.7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tuberculosis drugs; wastewater analysis; Chromatography; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e30720','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is a robust tool for disease surveillance and monitoring of pharmaceutical consumption. However, monitoring tuberculosis (TB) drug consumption faces challenges due to limited data availability. This study aimed to optimise methods for detecting TB drugs in treated and untreated wastewater from four African countries: South Africa, Nigeria, Kenya, and Cameroon. The limit of detection and limit of quantification varied among the target drugs and sites. Application of the optimised method for drug detection and quantification in both treated and untreated wastewater unveiled varied results, with ethambutol consistently most detected and pyrazinamide and isoniazid least detected.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(176,'药物类','抗生素','抗结核药物','利福平','结核病治疗（论文研究语境）','处方药','利福平','13292-46-1','分子量822.9 g/mol；LogP 2.95',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tuberculosis drugs; wastewater analysis; Chromatography; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e30720','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is a robust tool for disease surveillance and monitoring of pharmaceutical consumption. However, monitoring tuberculosis (TB) drug consumption faces challenges due to limited data availability. This study aimed to optimise methods for detecting TB drugs in treated and untreated wastewater from four African countries: South Africa, Nigeria, Kenya, and Cameroon. The limit of detection and limit of quantification varied among the target drugs and sites. Application of the optimised method for drug detection and quantification in both treated and untreated wastewater unveiled varied results, with ethambutol consistently most detected and pyrazinamide and isoniazid least detected.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(177,'药物类','消炎镇痛药','非甾体抗炎药','萘普生','疼痛管理；运动活动相关损伤疼痛','处方药','O-去甲基萘普生','52079-10-4','分子式C13H12O3；分子量216.23 g/mol',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE); COVID pandemics; Illicit drugs; Caffeine; Nicotine; Lifestyle; Human markers; Physical activity','10.1016/j.jhazmat.2024.134264','SARS-CoV-2 pandemic affected lifestyle habits, mental health and wellbeing. Two towns (Paulton and Radstock) and two cities (Bath and Bristol) in Southwest England were monitored for two years using wastewater-based epidemiology to assess impacts of COVID restriction measures on community lifestyle choices, including illicit drugs, legal stimulants, abused pharmaceuticals and pain pharma usage. Caffeine intake decreased after the third national lockdown, nicotine intake via cotinine remained stable, and pain pharma often used in pain management showed decreased usage due to restrictions in physical exercise and access to gyms/sport facilities.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(178,'药物类','精神神经类药物','苯二氮䓬类镇静/抗焦虑药','替马西泮','精神神经类药物（论文按psychoactive pharmaceuticals分组）','处方药','替马西泮','846-50-4','分子式C16H13ClN2O2；pKa 1.6；LogKow 2.19',1.340000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pharmaceutical usage; Wastewater treatment plant; Regional variation; Removal efficiency; Ecological risks','10.1016/j.envres.2024.118544','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) was used to estimate consumption of three cardiovascular, four non-steroidal anti-inflammatory, and four psychoactive pharmaceuticals between urban and suburban catchments in China. Eleven analytes were detected in influent and effluent samples. Estimated consumption ranges differed by pharmaceutical class and catchment type, and the study also evaluated removal efficiencies and ecological risks.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(179,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗抑郁药','文拉法辛','Antidepressants','处方药','O-去甲基文拉法辛','142761-11-3','分子式C16H25NO2；分子量273.44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Biomarkers; Pharmaceuticals; Wastewater; 2D-LC; Mass spectrometry; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.jpba.2021.114295','The biomarkers used in wastewater-based epidemiology studies have a wide range of physicochemical properties, making simultaneous analysis extremely challenging or even impossible. So far, the majority of analytical procedures employed in this field have focused on specific classes or a limited number of analytes. The heart-cutting two-dimensional liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry technique (2D-LC-MS/MS) has enabled the incorporation of compounds with significantly different polarities in a single analytical method. In this study, a 2D-LC-MS/MS method has been developed and optimized for the simultaneous analysis of various biomarkers in wastewater, providing relevant information about lifestyle habits (the usage of alcohol, tobacco, and caffeine), health and well-being (pharmaceuticals), and a population size biomarker (5-HIAA) that is useful for correct calculation of human population during wastewater-based epidemiology studies. A single-laboratory validation procedure showed satisfactory analytical performance, with the mean trueness for most compounds falling in the range of 80-110% and the mean repeatability being less than 20%. The applicability of the method was evaluated by testing 28 wastewater samples collected at different wastewater treatment plants in Latvia. The obtained results revealed the occurrence of 44 out of 62 selected biomarkers, with the lowest quantified concentration at 1.1 ng/L in the case of xylometazoline and up to 148 ug/L in the case of metformin and 156 ug/L for caffeine.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(180,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗癫痫/神经痛用药','卡马西平','Antiepileptic','处方药','卡马西平-10,11-环氧化物','36507-30-9','分子式C15H12N2O2；分子量252.27',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Biomarkers; Pharmaceuticals; Wastewater; 2D-LC; Mass spectrometry; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.jpba.2021.114295','The biomarkers used in wastewater-based epidemiology studies have a wide range of physicochemical properties, making simultaneous analysis extremely challenging or even impossible. So far, the majority of analytical procedures employed in this field have focused on specific classes or a limited number of analytes. The heart-cutting two-dimensional liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry technique (2D-LC-MS/MS) has enabled the incorporation of co