9-6','分子式 C21H25N；分子量 291.4 g/mol',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,27.0000,'Antidepressants; Wastewater-based epidemiology; Depression; Prevalence; Qinghai Province','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.163303','Wastewater-based epidemiology was used to estimate antidepressant consumption and depression prevalence in five cities of Qinghai Province, West China. Antidepressants were measured in influent and effluent wastewater from 17 wastewater treatment plants. Venlafaxine, desvenlafaxine, paroxetine, sertraline and nortriptyline were among the highest concentration quartile in influent samples. Back-calculation estimated venlafaxine, desvenlafaxine-based venlafaxine, paroxetine, sertraline and amitriptyline as the dominant consumption and prevalence contributors, and depression prevalence was estimated from antidepressant use prevalence.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(256,'药物类','泌尿/生殖系统药物','勃起功能障碍治疗药物','西地那非','勃起功能障碍','处方药','西地那非','171599-83-0','分子式 C22H30N6O4S；分子量 474.2；保留时间 4.55 min',17.500000,5.7000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sildenafil; Comorbidities; Lifestyles; Correlation; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.watres.2022.118446','Sildenafil (SIL) consumption and its associations with comorbidities and lifestyle factors were investigated using wastewater-based epidemiology in composite influent wastewater from 38 WWTPs in 33 Chinese cities. SIL consumption ranged from 10.6 to 132 mg/d/1000 people, prescription sales accounted for 13.3% of estimated SIL use in 2018, and SIL use was correlated with allopurinol, hydrochlorothiazide, nicotine, and alcohol use.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(257,'药物类','泌尿/生殖系统药物','勃起功能障碍治疗药物','西地那非','勃起功能障碍','处方药','去甲基西地那非','139755-82-1','分子式 C21H28N6O4S；分子量 460.55.；保留时间 4.55 min',12.000000,8.9000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sildenafil; Comorbidities; Lifestyles; Correlation; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.watres.2022.118446','Sildenafil (SIL) consumption and its associations with comorbidities and lifestyle factors were investigated using wastewater-based epidemiology in composite influent wastewater from 38 WWTPs in 33 Chinese cities. SIL consumption ranged from 10.6 to 132 mg/d/1000 people, prescription sales accounted for 13.3% of estimated SIL use in 2018, and SIL use was correlated with allopurinol, hydrochlorothiazide, nicotine, and alcohol use.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(258,'药物类','抗痛风药','黄嘌呤氧化酶抑制剂','别嘌醇','痛风/高尿酸血症','处方药','氧嘌呤醇','2465-59-0','分子式 C5H4N4O2；分子量 152.111；保留时间 1.36 min',1.370000,65.0000,21.8000,'g/d/1000 people',NULL,NULL,'Sildenafil; Comorbidities; Lifestyles; Correlation; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.watres.2022.118446','Sildenafil (SIL) consumption and its associations with comorbidities and lifestyle factors were investigated using wastewater-based epidemiology in composite influent wastewater from 38 WWTPs in 33 Chinese cities. SIL consumption ranged from 10.6 to 132 mg/d/1000 people, prescription sales accounted for 13.3% of estimated SIL use in 2018, and SIL use was correlated with allopurinol, hydrochlorothiazide, nicotine, and alcohol use.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(259,'药物类','阿片类药物','阿片类镇痛药','羟考酮','疼痛治疗','处方药','羟考酮','76-42-6','分子式 C18H21NO4；分子量 315.364；保留时间 1.57 min',11.200000,8.9000,3.0900,'mg/d/1000 people',NULL,NULL,'Sildenafil; Comorbidities; Lifestyles; Correlation; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.watres.2022.118446','Sildenafil (SIL) consumption and its associations with comorbidities and lifestyle factors were investigated using wastewater-based epidemiology in composite influent wastewater from 38 WWTPs in 33 Chinese cities. SIL consumption ranged from 10.6 to 132 mg/d/1000 people, prescription sales accounted for 13.3% of estimated SIL use in 2018, and SIL use was correlated with allopurinol, hydrochlorothiazide, nicotine, and alcohol use.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(260,'健康状态类','健康状态标志物','糖皮质激素','皮质醇','心理压力/应激水平评估','其他','皮质醇','50-23-7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater-based epidemiology; Hormones; Psychological stress; University campus; PSS questionnaire survey','10.1016/j.watres.2024.123022','This study evaluated cortisol and cortisone as wastewater biomarkers for psychological stress using small-scale campus DGT sampling and a large-scale municipal WWTP campaign in Dalian, China. Campus results showed higher cortisone mass loads during exam weeks and among females, consistent with PSS-14 questionnaire patterns, while municipal WWTP samples were more affected by seasonality, COVID-19, wastewater transport, and external pharmaceutical sources.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(261,'药物类','平喘药/呼吸系统用药','β受体激动剂','氯丙那林','支气管哮喘/肺部疾病','处方药','氯丙那林','3811-25-4',NULL,2.600000,39.0000,2.3400,'mg/1000 inh/day',NULL,NULL,'Beta-agonists; Wastewater-based epidemiology; Illegal usage; Risk assessment; Population model','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.164956','The illegal use of beta-agonists could cause severe problems to human health. In this study, the usage of beta-agonists in 31 cities across China was estimated using wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE). The proposed method is based on solid-phase extraction (SPE) and LC-MS/MS and was developed and validated to determine the concentration of seven beta-agonists in wastewater. A population model based on cotinine (COT), NH4-N and the flow volume was constructed to estimate the population equivalents for different wastewater treatment plants (WWTPs). Clenbuterol and ractopamine are banned in China for both animal husbandry and medical use, but were nevertheless detected in some wastewater samples at rates of 6.2 % and 4.7 %, respectively (n = 339). The WBE-based consumption of clenbuterol and ractopamine were compared with the acceptable daily intake (ADI) and the health risks were assessed by their hazard quotients. Salbutamol, clorprenaline and terbutaline were observed in practically all wastewater samples, whereas the formoterol and bambuterol concentrations were below the detection limit in all samples. Salbutamol consumption was highest among the examined beta-agonists and varied regionally.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(262,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','ACE抑制剂/降压药','依那普利','降压治疗','处方药','依那普利拉','76420-72-9',NULL,3.120000,34.6000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Urban wastewater; Pharmaceuticals; Compliance to treatment; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.139741','Sub-optimal adherence to pharmacological therapy is one of the main reasons for poor effectiveness, reducing the patient\'s quality of life and affecting health-care economics. This study investigated the possibility for a wastewater-based epidemiology approach to assess the overall adherence of a population to some pharmacological therapies in a defined area. Specific active ingredients and their main urinary metabolites were selected as biomarkers and measured in urban wastewater. The first case study was conducted in Italy, considering the whole country and two Italian regions by sampling for five days six cities from north to south. LC-MS/MS was used to measure biomarkers in raw wastewater. Concentrations in influent wastewater and reviewed excretion profiles were used to back-calculate measured consumption, which was compared with expected consumption from medical prescriptions reported by AIFA.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(263,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','ACE抑制剂/降压药','雷米普利','降压治疗','处方药','雷米普利拉','87269-97-4',NULL,10.930000,9.8000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Urban wastewater; Pharmaceuticals; Compliance to treatment; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.139741','Sub-optimal adherence to pharmacological therapy is one of the main reasons for poor effectiveness, reducing the patient\'s quality of life and affecting health-care economics. This study investigated the possibility for a wastewater-based epidemiology approach to assess the overall adherence of a population to some pharmacological therapies in a defined area. Specific active ingredients and their main urinary metabolites were selected as biomarkers and measured in urban wastewater. The first case study was conducted in Italy, considering the whole country and two Italian regions by sampling for five days six cities from north to south. LC-MS/MS was used to measure biomarkers in raw wastewater. Concentrations in influent wastewater and reviewed excretion profiles were used to back-calculate measured consumption, which was compared with expected consumption from medical prescriptions reported by AIFA.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(264,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗抑郁药','西酞普兰','抗抑郁治疗','处方药','N-去甲基西酞普兰','62498-67-3',NULL,9.810000,10.7000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Urban wastewater; Pharmaceuticals; Compliance to treatment; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.139741','Sub-optimal adherence to pharmacological therapy is one of the main reasons for poor effectiveness, reducing the patient\'s quality of life and affecting health-care economics. This study investigated the possibility for a wastewater-based epidemiology approach to assess the overall adherence of a population to some pharmacological therapies in a defined area. Specific active ingredients and their main urinary metabolites were selected as biomarkers and measured in urban wastewater. The first case study was conducted in Italy, considering the whole country and two Italian regions by sampling for five days six cities from north to south. LC-MS/MS was used to measure biomarkers in raw wastewater. Concentrations in influent wastewater and reviewed excretion profiles were used to back-calculate measured consumption, which was compared with expected consumption from medical prescriptions reported by AIFA.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(265,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','血管紧张素II受体阻滞剂','氯沙坦','降压治疗','处方药','EXP-3174','124750-92-1',NULL,18.390000,5.3000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Urban wastewater; Pharmaceuticals; Compliance to treatment; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.139741','Sub-optimal adherence to pharmacological therapy is one of the main reasons for poor effectiveness, reducing the patient\'s quality of life and affecting health-care economics. This study investigated the possibility for a wastewater-based epidemiology approach to assess the overall adherence of a population to some pharmacological therapies in a defined area. Specific active ingredients and their main urinary metabolites were selected as biomarkers and measured in urban wastewater. The first case study was conducted in Italy, considering the whole country and two Italian regions by sampling for five days six cities from north to south. LC-MS/MS was used to measure biomarkers in raw wastewater. Concentrations in influent wastewater and reviewed excretion profiles were used to back-calculate measured consumption, which was compared with expected consumption from medical prescriptions reported by AIFA.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(266,'药物类','精神神经类药物','镇静催眠/抗焦虑药','氟硝西泮','镇静催眠相关治疗','处方药','氟硝西泮','1622-62-4','分子式C16H12FN3O3；分子量313.28；logP 2.57',10.000000,10.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater-based epidemiology; Psychoactive drugs; Spatial distribution; Mental disorders','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.158982','Composite influent samples were collected from 26 wastewater treatment plants in 23 major cities in China. The concentrations of the psychoactive drugs diphenhydramine, fluoxetine, doxepin, imipramine, sulpiride, zolpidem, carbamazepine, and flunitrazepam in the wastewater were determined. Detection frequencies of diphenhydramine, sulpiride, and carbamazepine were close to 100%, whereas other compounds were lower than 35%. Carbamazepine had the highest mean consumption, followed by diphenhydramine and sulpiride. WBE estimates of average use were lower than drug statistics data. Correlations were examined between psychotropic drug use and illicit drugs, age, occupation, and obesity.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(267,'药物类','消炎镇痛药','非甾体抗炎药','塞来昔布','疼痛治疗/镇痛负担评估','处方药','塞来昔布','169590-42-5','分子式C17H14F3N3O2S；单同位素质量381.075867 Da',38.461538,2.6000,787320074.0000,'mg/day',NULL,NULL,'opioids; non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs; socioeconomics; pain; wastewater','10.1021/acs.est.2c06691','A wastewater-based epidemiology method was used to estimate analgesic consumption and assess treated pain burden in Australian communities. Wastewater influent samples from 60 communities representing about 52% of Australia\'s population were analyzed for analgesics, converted to drug consumed per day per 1000 inhabitants using pharmacokinetics and WBE data, and standardized to defined daily doses. The study compared non-opioid and opioid analgesic burden, socioeconomic factors, and national analgesic costs.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(268,'药物类','消炎镇痛药','非甾体抗炎药','布洛芬','疼痛治疗/镇痛负担评估','非处方药','布洛芬羧酸','15935-54-3','分子式C13H16O4；单同位素质量236.104858 Da',5.456912,16.0000,884334671.0000,'mg/day',NULL,NULL,'opioids; non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs; socioeconomics; pain; wastewater','10.1021/acs.est.2c06691','A wastewater-based epidemiology method was used to estimate analgesic consumption and assess treated pain burden in Australian communities. Wastewater influent samples from 60 communities representing about 52% of Australia\'s population were analyzed for analgesics, converted to drug consumed per day per 1000 inhabitants using pharmacokinetics and WBE data, and standardized to defined daily doses. The study compared non-opioid and opioid analgesic burden, socioeconomic factors, and national analgesic costs.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(269,'药物类','阿片类药物','阿片维持治疗药物','美沙酮','疼痛治疗/镇痛负担评估','处方药','美沙酮；EDDP','17109-49-8','美沙酮: 分子式C21H27NO；单同位素质量309.209259 Da；EDDP: 分子式C20H23N；单同位素质量277.183044 Da',NULL,5.0000,11431882.0000,'mg/day',NULL,NULL,'opioids; non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs; socioeconomics; pain; wastewater','10.1021/acs.est.2c