119-62-0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WBE; antibiotics; antivirals; antimicrobial resistance; prescription; data triangulation; direct disposal','10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.131461','本研究在英国西南部 Bath 与 Keynsham 两个社区污水汇水区开展13个月纵向 WBE 研究，用24 h流量比例复合进水样监测抗微生物药及代谢物的污水负荷，并将污水估算摄入量与 catchment 处方数据、人口数据进行比较。','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(373,'药物类','抗生素','二氨基嘧啶类','甲氧苄啶','感染性疾病治疗/抗微生物用药监测','处方药','4-羟基甲氧苄啶','112678-48-5',NULL,24.770000,NULL,8.4040,'mg/day/1000 inh',NULL,NULL,'WBE; antibiotics; antivirals; antimicrobial resistance; prescription; data triangulation; direct disposal','10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.131461','本研究在英国西南部 Bath 与 Keynsham 两个社区污水汇水区开展13个月纵向 WBE 研究，用24 h流量比例复合进水样监测抗微生物药及代谢物的污水负荷，并将污水估算摄入量与 catchment 处方数据、人口数据进行比较。','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(374,'药物类','抗生素','林可酰胺类代谢物','克林霉素','感染性疾病治疗/抗微生物用药监测','处方药','N-去甲基克林霉素','22431-45-4',NULL,19.620000,NULL,29.9552,'mg/day/1000 inh',NULL,NULL,'WBE; antibiotics; antivirals; antimicrobial resistance; prescription; data triangulation; direct disposal','10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.131461','本研究在英国西南部 Bath 与 Keynsham 两个社区污水汇水区开展13个月纵向 WBE 研究，用24 h流量比例复合进水样监测抗微生物药及代谢物的污水负荷，并将污水估算摄入量与 catchment 处方数据、人口数据进行比较。','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(375,'药物类','抗生素','碳青霉烯类抗菌药','亚胺培南','感染性疾病治疗/抗微生物用药监测','处方药','亚胺培南','64221-86-9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WBE; antibiotics; antivirals; antimicrobial resistance; prescription; data triangulation; direct disposal','10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.131461','本研究在英国西南部 Bath 与 Keynsham 两个社区污水汇水区开展13个月纵向 WBE 研究，用24 h流量比例复合进水样监测抗微生物药及代谢物的污水负荷，并将污水估算摄入量与 catchment 处方数据、人口数据进行比较。','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(376,'暴露/生活方式标志物','膳食/营养标志物','维生素B6代谢标志物','维生素B6','人口模型标志物；不代表药物治疗适应症','其他','4-吡哆酸','82-82-6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Multi-parameter population model; Endogenous population biomarkers; Wastewater epidemiology; PPCPs','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.143480','The consumption or prevalence of acesulfame, caffeine, paracetamol and amantadine was estimated by wastewater-based epidemiology based on a multi-parameter population model in 20 sewage treatment plants (STPs) in Hebei province, China. To minimize the uncertainties contributed by population estimation in WBE, a multi-parameter population model was established based on population biomarker equivalent population and flow volume-population with weight factors calculated by the analytic hierarchy process. 4-Pyridoxic acid (4-PA), cotinine, trans-3\'-hydroxycotinine and 1,4-methylimidazole acetic acid (MIAA) were selected as population biomarkers. The estimated model population showed high correlation with census data. Estimated consumption of acesulfame, caffeine, paracetamol and amantadine was 6.7 +/- 2.4, 50.5 +/- 38.5, 61.5 +/- 52.7 and 0.52 +/- 0.33 mg/day/inh, respectively, and prevalence of paracetamol and amantadine was 5.3% +/- 4.5% and 0.28% +/- 0.18%, respectively.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(377,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗帕金森药/抗病毒药','金刚烷胺','anti-influenza A virus；Parkinson\'s disease','处方药','金刚烷胺','768-94-5',NULL,1.100000,90.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Multi-parameter population model; Endogenous population biomarkers; Wastewater epidemiology; PPCPs','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.143480','The consumption or prevalence of acesulfame, caffeine, paracetamol and amantadine was estimated by wastewater-based epidemiology based on a multi-parameter population model in 20 sewage treatment plants (STPs) in Hebei province, China. To minimize the uncertainties contributed by population estimation in WBE, a multi-parameter population model was established based on population biomarker equivalent population and flow volume-population with weight factors calculated by the analytic hierarchy process. 4-Pyridoxic acid (4-PA), cotinine, trans-3\'-hydroxycotinine and 1,4-methylimidazole acetic acid (MIAA) were selected as population biomarkers. The estimated model population showed high correlation with census data. Estimated consumption of acesulfame, caffeine, paracetamol and amantadine was 6.7 +/- 2.4, 50.5 +/- 38.5, 61.5 +/- 52.7 and 0.52 +/- 0.33 mg/day/inh, respectively, and prevalence of paracetamol and amantadine was 5.3% +/- 4.5% and 0.28% +/- 0.18%, respectively.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(378,'暴露/生活方式标志物','植物/中药暴露标志物','马兜铃酸类/马兜铃内酰胺类','含马兜铃酸中药/草本毒性成分暴露','中药毒性成分暴露评估；不代表治疗适应症','其他','马兜铃酸I','313-67-7','论文说明 AA-I/AL-I 来源于 Aristolochia 物种，AA-I 为马兜铃酸类毒性成分，AL-I 为其代谢物，具有肾毒性和致癌性；未给结构化理化参数。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1039/d5ay01417d','Aristolochic acid I (AA-I) and its metabolite aristolactam I (AL-I) are nephrotoxic and carcinogenic compounds derived from Aristolochia species. This study developed and validated a UPLC-MS/MS method for AA-I and AL-I across Chinese herbal decoctions, human urine, river water, and influent and effluent from a municipal wastewater treatment plant. Application of the method showed high AA-I in one herbal decoction, urinary AL-I after ingestion, and consistent AL-I detection in influent wastewater, demonstrating the feasibility of wastewater-based epidemiology for population exposure assessment of toxic herbal constituents.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(379,'暴露/生活方式标志物','植物/中药暴露标志物','马兜铃酸类/马兜铃内酰胺类','含马兜铃酸中药/草本毒性成分暴露','中药毒性成分暴露评估；不代表治疗适应症','其他','马兜铃内酰胺I','13395-02-3','论文说明 AA-I/AL-I 来源于 Aristolochia 物种，AA-I 为马兜铃酸类毒性成分，AL-I 为其代谢物，具有肾毒性和致癌性；未给结构化理化参数。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1039/d5ay01417d','Aristolochic acid I (AA-I) and its metabolite aristolactam I (AL-I) are nephrotoxic and carcinogenic compounds derived from Aristolochia species. This study developed and validated a UPLC-MS/MS method for AA-I and AL-I across Chinese herbal decoctions, human urine, river water, and influent and effluent from a municipal wastewater treatment plant. Application of the method showed high AA-I in one herbal decoction, urinary AL-I after ingestion, and consistent AL-I detection in influent wastewater, demonstrating the feasibility of wastewater-based epidemiology for population exposure assessment of toxic herbal constituents.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(380,'消费类','烟草','尼古丁及代谢物','尼古丁',NULL,'其他','可替宁葡萄糖醛酸苷','139427-57-9','尼古丁II相代谢物（O-葡萄糖醛酸苷）；分子式C16H20N2O7；分子量352.343 g/mol；logKow -2.75；pKa 2.85 -1.2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Food biomarkers; LC-MS/MS; Method development; Stability; Wastewater analysis; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1007/s00216-026-06495-1','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is increasingly used to assess the consumption of illicit drugs and other lifestyle chemicals, while its potential for evaluating population dietary habits has been scarcely investigated. In this study, a multi-residue analytical method was developed to determine more than 40 lifestyle and dietary biomarkers in raw municipal wastewater. In addition to biomarkers commonly included in WBE studies, this method incorporates several food biomarkers not previously analysed in this context. The target biomarkers were analysed using ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry. Optimal separation was achieved on an ACQUITY UPLC HSS T3 column using gradient elution with 0.1% acetic acid and acetonitrile, while multiple reaction monitoring mode was used for detection and quantification of the target compounds. Sample preparation involved solid-phase extraction (SPE) on hydrophilic-lipophilic cartridges for biomarkers present at lower concentrations in wastewater (mainly food biomarkers), while direct injection of diluted wastewater samples was used for other analytes, including alcohol and tobacco/nicotine biomarkers, artificial sweeteners, antidiabetic metformin, certain vitamins, and a few other food biomarkers. The method validation parameters, including SPE recovery and accuracy, were acceptable in most cases, and the method sensitivity was sufficient to enable reliable determination of the target biomarkers in real samples. Regarding stability in wastewater during sample collection and storage, most biomarkers remained stable at 4 °C for 24 h, but moderate to high loss of some analytes occurred during the freeze-thaw cycle. The method\'s applicability was verified using 24-h wastewater samples from four Croatian cities, confirming its suitability for WBE.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(381,'消费类','烟草','烟草消费标志物','烟草消费',NULL,'其他','新烟碱','53912-89-3','烟草生物碱；分子式C10H14N2；分子量162.236 g/mol；logKow 1.52；pKa 9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Food biomarkers; LC-MS/MS; Method development; Stability; Wastewater analysis; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1007/s00216-026-06495-1','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is increasingly used to assess the consumption of illicit drugs and other lifestyle chemicals, while its potential for evaluating population dietary habits has been scarcely investigated. In this study, a multi-residue analytical method was developed to determine more than 40 lifestyle and dietary biomarkers in raw municipal wastewater. In addition to biomarkers commonly included in WBE studies, this method incorporates several food biomarkers not previously analysed in this context. The target biomarkers were analysed using ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry. Optimal separation was achieved on an ACQUITY UPLC HSS T3 column using gradient elution with 0.1% acetic acid and acetonitrile, while multiple reaction monitoring mode was used for detection and quantification of the target compounds. Sample preparation involved solid-phase extraction (SPE) on hydrophilic-lipophilic cartridges for biomarkers present at lower concentrations in wastewater (mainly food biomarkers), while direct injection of diluted wastewater samples was used for other analytes, including alcohol and tobacco/nicotine biomarkers, artificial sweeteners, antidiabetic metformin, certain vitamins, and a few other food biomarkers. The method validation parameters, including SPE recovery and accuracy, were acceptable in most cases, and the method sensitivity was sufficient to enable reliable determination of the target biomarkers in real samples. Regarding stability in wastewater during sample collection and storage, most biomarkers remained stable at 4 °C for 24 h, but moderate to high loss of some analytes occurred during the freeze-thaw cycle. The method\'s applicability was verified using 24-h wastewater samples from four Croatian cities, confirming its suitability for WBE.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(382,'药物类','抗糖尿病药','双胍类','二甲双胍','糖尿病治疗','处方药','二甲双胍','1115-70-4','双胍类抗糖尿病药；分子式C4H11N5；分子量129.167 g/mol；logKow -0.75；pKa 12.33',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Food biomarkers; LC-MS/MS; Method development; Stability; Wastewater analysis; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1007/s00216-026-06495-1','Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is increasingly used to assess the consumption of illicit drugs and other lifestyle chemicals, while its potential for evaluating population dietary habits has been scarcely investigated. In this study, a multi-residue analytical method was developed to determine more than 40 lifestyle and dietary biomarkers in raw municipal wastewater. In addition to biomarkers commonly included in WBE studies, this method incorporates several food biomarkers not previously analysed in this context. The target biomarkers were analysed using ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry. Optimal separation was achieved on an ACQUITY UPLC HSS T3 column using gradient elution with 0.1% acetic acid and acetonitrile, while multiple reaction monitoring mode was used for detection and quantification of the target compounds. Sample preparation involved solid-phase extraction (SPE) on hydrophilic-lipophilic cartridges for biomarkers present at lower concentrations in wastewater (mainly food biomarkers), while direct injection of diluted wastewater samples was used for other analytes, including alcohol and tobacco/nicotine biomarkers, artificial sweeteners, antidiabetic metformin, certain vitamins, and a few other food biomarkers. The method validation parameters, including SPE recovery and accuracy, were acceptable in most cases, and the method sensitivity was sufficient to enable reliable determination of the target biomarkers in real samples. Regarding stability in wastewater during sample collection and storage, most biomarkers remained stable at 4 °C for 24 h, but moderate to high loss of some analytes occurred during the freeze-thaw cycle. The method\'s applicability was verified using 24-h wastewater samples from four Croatian cities, confirming its suitability for WBE.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(383,'药物类','泌尿/生殖系统药物','勃起功能障碍治疗药物','西地那非','勃起功能障碍','处方药','去乙基西地那非','139755-91-2','分子式 C20H28O4N6S；log Kow 1.99；西地那非主要转化/代谢产物。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater-based epidemiology; Phosphodiesterase type V inhibitors; Prescription pharmaceuticals; Tandem mass spectrometry','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2016.04.158','A simple, fast and reliable analytical method for the determination of phosphodiesterase type V inhibitors Received 4 March 2016 in wastewater was developed and validated. The method was based on direct injection followed by liquid Received in revised form 15 April 2016 chromatography coupled to tandem mass spectrometry with triple quadrupole as mass analyzer. Transformation Accepted 22 April 2016 products and analogues were included in the target list besides the three active pharmaceutical ingredients Available online 7 May 2016 (sildenafil, vardenafil and tadalafil). The method performance was thoroughly investigated, including the analyte stability in wastewater and matrix effect. All target compounds presented linear fits between Keywords: their LOD and 500 ng/L. The quantification limits ranged from 1.6 to 30 ng/L for all compounds except for Wastewater-based epidemiology Phosphodiesterase type V inhibitors n-octylnortadalafil (LOQ: 100 ng/L); precision calculated as intraday repeatability was lower than 30%; accuracy Prescription pharmaceuticals calculated as procedural recovery ranged successfully between 85 and 105% in all cases. The method was applied Tandem mass spectrometry to samples collected during three week-long monitoring campaigns performed in 2013, 2014 and 2015 in three Dutch cities. Only sildenafil and its two metabolites, desmethyl- and desethylsildenafil, were present with normal- ized loads ranging from LOQ to 8.3, 11.8 and 21.6 mg/day/1000 inh, respectively. Two additional week-long sets of samples were collected in Amsterdam at the time that a festival event took place, bringing around 350,000 visitors to the city. The difference in drug usage patterns was statistically studied: “weekday” versus “weekend”, “normal” versus “atypical” week; and results discussed. The metabolite to parent drug concentration ratio evolution during consecutive years was discussed, leading to several possible explanations that should be further investigated. Finally, wastewater-based epidemiology approach was applied to back-calculate sildenafil consumption.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(384,'药物类','平喘药/呼吸系统用药','镇咳药','右美沙芬','缓解干咳症状','非处方药','右啡烷','125-73-5','分子式C17H23NO；分子量257',1.700000,62.5000,12.7000,'mg/day/1000 inh',NULL,NULL,'Dextromethorphan; Dextrorphan; Cough suppressant biomarker; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.watres.2025.124119','Coughing often signals respiratory health issues. The use of dextromethorphan, available as an over-the-counter opioid antitussive in China, is largely undocumented. This study evaluates the feasibility of dextromethorphan and its metabolite dextrorphan as wastewater-based epidemiology biomarkers for monitoring dextromethorphan use. Both dextromethorphan and dextrorphan are excreted via urine (62.5% as dextrorphan and 0.5% as dextromethorphan), were measured in wastewater, and were deemed stable over 72 h. Using dextrorphan as the WBE biomarker, the study assessed temporal and spatial dextromethorphan usage trends across 30 Chinese cities and Dalian, supporting WBE monitoring of population-level respiratory OTC medication use.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(385,'消费类','烟草','尼古丁及代谢物','尼古丁',NULL,'其他','anatabine（阿那他宾）','581-49-7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'wastewater-based epidemiology; tobacco; tobacco-specific nitrosamines; cotinine; LC-MS/MS','10.1021/acs.analchem.7b02052','This study developed and validated an LC-MS/MS method for tobacco-related alkaloids, tobacco-specific nitrosamines and metabolites in raw wastewater, then applied it to 24-h composite influent wastewater samples from Geraardsbergen and Ninove, Belgium. COT, COT-OH, ANATA, ANABA and NAT were found in wastewater, while NAB, NNN, NNK and NNAL were not quantifiable.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(386,'消费类','烟草','尼古丁及代谢物','尼古丁',NULL,'其他','anabasine（阿那巴辛）','494-52-0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'wastewater-based epidemiology; tobacco; tobacco-specific nitrosamines; cotinine; LC-MS/MS','10.1021/acs.analchem.7b02052','This study developed and validated an LC-MS/MS method for tobacco-related alkaloids, tobacco-specific nitrosamines and metabolites in raw wastewater, then applied it to 24-h composite influent wastewater samples from Geraardsbergen and Ninove, Belgium. COT, COT-OH, ANATA, ANABA and NAT were found in wastewater, while NAB, NNN, NNK and NNAL were not quantifiable.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(387,'消费类','烟草','尼古丁及代谢物','尼古丁',NULL,'其他','N-亚硝基阿那他宾','71267-22-6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'wastewater-based epidemiology; tobacco; tobacco-specific nitrosamines; cotinine; LC-MS/MS','10.1021/acs.analchem.7b02052','This study developed and validated an LC-MS/MS method for tobacco-related alkaloids, tobacco-specific nitrosamines and metabolites in raw wastewater, then applied it to 24-h composite influent wastewater samples from Geraardsbergen and Ninove, Belgium. COT, COT-OH, ANATA, ANABA and NAT were found in wastewater, while NAB, NNN, NNK and NNAL were not quantifiable.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(388,'药物类','阿片类药物','阿片类镇痛药','曲马多','镇痛','处方药','N-去甲基曲马多','75377-45-6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater based epidemiology; Risk characterisation; Daily load; Emerging contaminants; Wastewater treatment works','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.160254','The study evaluated the presence and fate of various contaminants of emerging concern (CECs) from a South African wastewater treatment works (WWTW) and surface waters located around an urban setting. A total of 45 CECs were quantified from nine sampling locations over an 11-month period. Daily loads of the target analytes in the WWTW showed persistence of some CECs, along with population-normalised daily loads of pharmaceuticals and drugs of abuse that were estimated for the first time in the study area. Multiple chemical markers were recorded in river water upstream of the WWTW discharge, suggesting diffuse pollution from urban communities not connected to sewage networks or where sanitation services are limited. The potential of using defined surface water locations to perform community-wide substance use profiling for non-sewered communities was explored. Environmental risk characterisation for WWTW effluent and surface waters provided risk quotients and frequencies of exceedance for the target CECs. The study highlighted challenges and limitations associated with applying wastewater-based epidemiology in non-sewered communities.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(389,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗癫痫/神经痛用药','卡马西平','抗癫痫','处方药','10,11-二氢-11-羟基卡马西平','29331-92-8',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater based epidemiology; Risk characterisation; Daily load; Emerging contaminants; Wastewater treatment works','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.160254','The study evaluated the presence and fate of various contaminants of emerging concern (CECs) from a South African wastewater treatment works (WWTW) and surface waters located around an urban setting. A total of 45 CECs were quantified from nine sampling locations over an 11-month period. Daily loads of the target analytes in the WWTW showed persistence of some CECs, along with population-normalised daily loads of pharmaceuticals and drugs of abuse that were estimated for the first time in the study area. Multiple chemical markers were recorded in river water upstream of the WWTW discharge, suggesting diffuse pollution from urban communities not connected to sewage networks or where sanitation services are limited. The potential of using defined surface water locations to perform community-wide substance use profiling for non-sewered communities was explored. Environmental risk characterisation for WWTW effluent and surface waters provided risk quotients and frequencies of exceedance for the target CECs. The study highlighted challenges and limitations associated with applying wastewater-based epidemiology in non-sewered communities.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(390,'药物类','抗消化性溃疡药','H2受体拮抗剂','西咪替丁','胃部疾病治疗','非处方药','西咪替丁','51481-61-9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater based epidemiology; Risk characterisation; Daily load; Emerging contaminants; Wastewater treatment works','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.160254','The study evaluated the presence and fate of various contaminants of emerging concern (CECs) from a South African wastewater treatment works (WWTW) and surface waters located around an urban setting. A total of 45 CECs were quantified from nine sampling locations over an 11-month period. Daily loads of the target analytes in the WWTW showed persistence of some CECs, along with population-normalised daily loads of pharmaceuticals and drugs of abuse that were estimated for the first time in the study area. Multiple chemical markers were recorded in river water upstream of the WWTW discharge, suggesting diffuse pollution from urban communities not connected to sewage networks or where sanitation services are limited. The potential of using defined surface water locations to perform community-wide substance use profiling for non-sewered communities was explored. Environmental risk characterisation for WWTW effluent and surface waters provided risk quotients and frequencies of exceedance for the target CECs. The study highlighted challenges and limitations associated with applying wastewater-based epidemiology in non-sewered communities.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(391,'健康状态类','健康状态标志物','糖皮质激素','人群压力/健康状态','人群压力和健康状态监测','其他','总糖皮质激素（皮质醇+可的松）','50-23-7; 53-06-5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wastewater-based epidemiology; Cortisol; Cortisone; College campus; Students; Stability study','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.155961','Stress is oftentimes overlooked in societies, despite its life-threatening impact. This study assessed the feasibility of measuring endogenous stress hormones to estimate population-level stress by wastewater-based epidemiology. Two primary glucocorticoids, cortisol and cortisone, were monitored in wastewater by LC-MS/MS to assess changes in physiological markers of stress in a student population (n = 26,000 +/- 7100) on a university campus in the southwestern U.S. Daily composite samples were collected for seven consecutive days each month during the Fall 2017 and Spring 2018 academic semesters. Reproducible weekly patterns were seen in stress hormone excretion, with higher levels on weekdays than weekends and higher per-person levels during the first two months of each semester. Overall Spring semester stress levels were significantly higher than Fall. The study demonstrated the utility of endogenous glucocorticoid biomarkers to monitor population health status, in this case community stress, in near real time by wastewater assessments.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(392,'药物类','抗生素','β-内酰胺类/青霉素类','阿莫西林酸',NULL,'处方药','阿莫西林酸','42947-63-7','分子式C16H21N3O6S；logP -4.6（SI Table S1）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial resistance; Antibiotic; Environmental risk assessment; Public health; One Health','10.1016/j.envint.2025.109606','Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major public health concern. Antimicrobial residues enter wastewater where their continued presence can lead to an increased risk of AMR while also causing environmental harm when untreated wastewater is discharged into the environment. This research presents the antimicrobial residue surveillance results of a national-scale wastewater sampling campaign across Wales. Wastewater from 15 sites - effluent from 7 hospitals and influent from 8 community wastewater treatment plants - was collected for 5 consecutive days monthly from May to July 2023. Using UPLC-MS/MS, over 175 unique wastewater samples were analyzed for more than 40 antimicrobials including beta-lactams, macrolides, quinolones, sulfonamides, a veterinary antibiotic, an antifungal, antivirals, and numerous metabolites. Several antimicrobials remained at high-risk concentrations even after dilution in community wastewater, demonstrating the need for regular monitoring of AMR and environmental risk posed by antimicrobials in wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(393,'药物类','抗生素','β-内酰胺类','美西林',NULL,'处方药','美西林','32887-01-7','分子式C15H23N3O3S；logP 2.1（SI Table S1）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial resistance; Antibiotic; Environmental risk assessment; Public health; One Health','10.1016/j.envint.2025.109606','Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major public health concern. Antimicrobial residues enter wastewater where their continued presence can lead to an increased risk of AMR while also causing environmental harm when untreated wastewater is discharged into the environment. This research presents the antimicrobial residue surveillance results of a national-scale wastewater sampling campaign across Wales. Wastewater from 15 sites - effluent from 7 hospitals and influent from 8 commun