gn across Wales. Wastewater from 15 sites - effluent from 7 hospitals and influent from 8 community wastewater treatment plants - was collected for 5 consecutive days monthly from May to July 2023. Using UPLC-MS/MS, over 175 unique wastewater samples were analyzed for more than 40 antimicrobials including beta-lactams, macrolides, quinolones, sulfonamides, a veterinary antibiotic, an antifungal, antivirals, and numerous metabolites. Several antimicrobials remained at high-risk concentrations even after dilution in community wastewater, demonstrating the need for regular monitoring of AMR and environmental risk posed by antimicrobials in wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(397,'药物类','抗生素','糖肽类','万古霉素',NULL,'处方药','万古霉素','1404-90-6','分子式C66H75Cl2N9O24；logP -2.6（SI Table S1）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial resistance; Antibiotic; Environmental risk assessment; Public health; One Health','10.1016/j.envint.2025.109606','Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major public health concern. Antimicrobial residues enter wastewater where their continued presence can lead to an increased risk of AMR while also causing environmental harm when untreated wastewater is discharged into the environment. This research presents the antimicrobial residue surveillance results of a national-scale wastewater sampling campaign across Wales. Wastewater from 15 sites - effluent from 7 hospitals and influent from 8 community wastewater treatment plants - was collected for 5 consecutive days monthly from May to July 2023. Using UPLC-MS/MS, over 175 unique wastewater samples were analyzed for more than 40 antimicrobials including beta-lactams, macrolides, quinolones, sulfonamides, a veterinary antibiotic, an antifungal, antivirals, and numerous metabolites. Several antimicrobials remained at high-risk concentrations even after dilution in community wastewater, demonstrating the need for regular monitoring of AMR and environmental risk posed by antimicrobials in wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(398,'药物类','抗生素','硝基咪唑类','甲硝唑',NULL,'处方药','羟基甲硝唑','4812-40-2','分子式C6H9N3O4；logP -1.3（SI Table S1）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial resistance; Antibiotic; Environmental risk assessment; Public health; One Health','10.1016/j.envint.2025.109606','Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major public health concern. Antimicrobial residues enter wastewater where their continued presence can lead to an increased risk of AMR while also causing environmental harm when untreated wastewater is discharged into the environment. This research presents the antimicrobial residue surveillance results of a national-scale wastewater sampling campaign across Wales. Wastewater from 15 sites - effluent from 7 hospitals and influent from 8 community wastewater treatment plants - was collected for 5 consecutive days monthly from May to July 2023. Using UPLC-MS/MS, over 175 unique wastewater samples were analyzed for more than 40 antimicrobials including beta-lactams, macrolides, quinolones, sulfonamides, a veterinary antibiotic, an antifungal, antivirals, and numerous metabolites. Several antimicrobials remained at high-risk concentrations even after dilution in community wastewater, demonstrating the need for regular monitoring of AMR and environmental risk posed by antimicrobials in wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(399,'药物类','抗生素','喹诺酮类','氧氟沙星',NULL,'处方药','氧氟沙星N-氧化物','104721-52-0','分子式C18H20FN3O5；logP 1.3（SI Table S1）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial resistance; Antibiotic; Environmental risk assessment; Public health; One Health','10.1016/j.envint.2025.109606','Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major public health concern. Antimicrobial residues enter wastewater where their continued presence can lead to an increased risk of AMR while also causing environmental harm when untreated wastewater is discharged into the environment. This research presents the antimicrobial residue surveillance results of a national-scale wastewater sampling campaign across Wales. Wastewater from 15 sites - effluent from 7 hospitals and influent from 8 community wastewater treatment plants - was collected for 5 consecutive days monthly from May to July 2023. Using UPLC-MS/MS, over 175 unique wastewater samples were analyzed for more than 40 antimicrobials including beta-lactams, macrolides, quinolones, sulfonamides, a veterinary antibiotic, an antifungal, antivirals, and numerous metabolites. Several antimicrobials remained at high-risk concentrations even after dilution in community wastewater, demonstrating the need for regular monitoring of AMR and environmental risk posed by antimicrobials in wastewater.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(400,'药物类','抗生素','β-内酰胺类/青霉素类','Ampicillin','治疗感染性疾病','处方药','Ampicillin','69-53-4','分子式C16H19N3O4S；分子量349.40 Da（SI Table S5）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whole-genome sequencing; Land use; Carbapenemase-producing enterobacteriaceae; ESBL-producing E. coli; Sewer system survey','10.1016/j.watres.2025.124136','The prevalence of antibiotic-resistant bacteria (ARB) poses a significant threat to public health. This study surveyed wastewater at 33 municipal sewer access sites in a city in Japan during January 2022 to March 2024 to assess antibiotic resistance status. Concentrations of antibiotic-resistant E. coli and antibiotics were quantified, urban land-use zones of sewer catchments were summarized, and whole-genome sequencing was used to investigate ESBL-EC and CPE. Sewer samples shared similar antibiotic resistance profiles with influent of five downstream wastewater treatment plants. Levofloxacin and sulfamethoxazole concentrations were correlated positively with antibiotic-resistant E. coli concentrations in the sewer system.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(401,'药物类','抗生素','喹诺酮类','左氧氟沙星','治疗感染性疾病','处方药','左氧氟沙星','100986-85-4','分子式C18H20FN3O4；分子量361.37 Da（SI Table S5）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,