026-06-15 20:40:21'),(403,'药物类','抗生素','酰胺醇类','甲砜霉素','治疗感染性疾病','处方药','甲砜霉素','15318-45-3','分子式C12H15Cl2NO5S；分子量356.21 Da（SI Table S5）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whole-genome sequencing; Land use; Carbapenemase-producing enterobacteriaceae; ESBL-producing E. coli; Sewer system survey','10.1016/j.watres.2025.124136','The prevalence of antibiotic-resistant bacteria (ARB) poses a significant threat to public health. This study surveyed wastewater at 33 municipal sewer access sites in a city in Japan during January 2022 to March 2024 to assess antibiotic resistance status. Concentrations of antibiotic-resistant E. coli and antibiotics were quantified, urban land-use zones of sewer catchments were summarized, and whole-genome sequencing was used to investigate ESBL-EC and CPE. Sewer samples shared similar antibiotic resistance profiles with influent of five downstream wastewater treatment plants. Levofloxacin and sulfamethoxazole concentrations were correlated positively with antibiotic-resistant E. coli concentrations in the sewer system.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(404,'药物类','抗生素','磺胺类','磺胺单甲氧嘧啶','治疗感染性疾病','处方药','磺胺单甲氧嘧啶','1220-83-3','分子式C11H12N4O3S；分子量280.06 Da（SI Table S5）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whole-genome sequencing; Land use; Carbapenemase-producing enterobacteriaceae; ESBL-producing E. coli; Sewer system survey','10.1016/j.watres.2025.124136','The prevalence of antibiotic-resistant bacteria (ARB) poses a significant threat to public health. This study surveyed wastewater at 33 municipal sewer access sites in a city in Japan during January 2022 to March 2024 to assess antibiotic resistance status. Concentrations of antibiotic-resistant E. coli and antibiotics were quantified, urban land-use zones of sewer catchments were summarized, and whole-genome sequencing was used to investigate ESBL-EC and CPE. Sewer samples shared similar antibiotic resistance profiles with influent of five downstream wastewater treatment plants. Levofloxacin and sulfamethoxazole concentrations were correlated positively with antibiotic-resistant E. coli concentrations in the sewer system.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(405,'药物类','抗生素','硝基呋喃类代谢物','呋喃妥因','抗微生物/抗感染用药','处方药','1-(2-硝基苄叉氨基)-2,4-咪唑烷二酮','623145-57-3','分子式C10H8N4O4；单同位素质量248.05（SI Table S1）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial agent; Informal settlement; Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE); Daily (per capita) intake; Antibiotics; Antifungals','10.1016/j.watres.2023.120110','There has been a significant increase in antimicrobial agents (AAs) usage globally, but relative consumption is unevenly distributed between nations. Inappropriate antibiotic use can contribute to antimicrobial resistance, so community-wide prescribing and consumption behaviours need monitoring. This study used wastewater-based epidemiology / urban water fingerprinting in Stellenbosch, South Africa, to back-calculate antimicrobial intake from quantities measured in municipal wastewater and informal settlement discharge. Seventeen antimicrobials and their human metabolites were evaluated against catchment prescription records. Proportional excretion, biological/chemical stability and method recovery were important for the calculations, and mass-per-day measurements were normalized by population estimates. Municipal WWTP estimates were used for wastewater and prescription data normalization, while informal settlement population estimates were less certain. Mass loads and normalized loads indicated higher relative usage in settlements for several compounds, and UWF data triangulation with prescription datasets showed good correlations for some antimicrobials while revealing discrepancies for others. The paper concludes that WBE/UWF can provide a comprehensive epidemiological tool for tracking pharmaceutical usage where prescription records are incomplete.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(406,'药物类','抗生素','喹诺酮类','诺氟沙星','抗微生物/抗感染用药','处方药','羟基诺氟沙星','109142-49-6','分子式C16H18FN3O4；单同位素质量335.13（SI Table S1）',1904.571616,0.0500,2624.3126,'mg/day/1000 inh',NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial agent; Informal settlement; Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE); Daily (per capita) intake; Antibiotics; Antifungals','10.1016/j.watres.2023.120110','There has been a significant increase in antimicrobial agents (AAs) usage globally, but relative consumption is unevenly distributed between nations. Inappropriate antibiotic use can contribute to antimicrobial resistance, so community-wide prescribing and consumption behaviours need monitoring. This study used wastewater-based epidemiology / urban water fingerprinting in Stellenbosch, South Africa, to back-calculate antimicrobial intake from quantities measured in municipal wastewater and informal settlement discharge. Seventeen antimicrobials and their human metabolites were evaluated against catchment prescription records. Proportional excretion, biological/chemical stability and method recovery were important for the calculations, and mass-per-day measurements were normalized by population estimates. Municipal WWTP estimates were used for wastewater and prescription data normalization, while informal settlement population estimates were less certain. Mass loads and normalized loads indicated higher relative usage in settlements for several compounds, and UWF data triangulation with prescription datasets showed good correlations for some antimicrobials while revealing discrepancies for others. The paper concludes that WBE/UWF can provide a comprehensive epidemiological tool for tracking pharmaceutical usage where prescription records are incomplete.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(407,'药物类','抗生素','硝基呋喃类','呋喃妥因','抗微生物/抗感染用药','处方药','呋喃妥因','67-20-9','分子式C8H6N4O5；单同位素质量238.03（SI Table S1）',2.899706,34.4900,27.6950,'mg/day/1000 inh',NULL,NULL,'Antimicrobial agent; Informal settlement; Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE); Daily (per capita) intake; Antibiotics; Antifungals','10.1016/j.watres.2023.120110','There has been a significant increase in antimicrobial agents (AAs) usage globally, but relative consumption is unevenly distributed between nations. Inappropriate antibiotic use can contribute to antimicrobial resistance, so community-wide prescribing and consumption behaviours need monitoring. This study used wastewater-based epidemiology / urban water fingerprinting in Stellenbosch, South Africa, to back-calculate antimicrobial intake from quantities measured in municipal wastewater and informal settlement discharge. Seventeen antimicrobials and their human metabolites were evaluated against catchment prescription records. Proportional excretion, biological/chemical stability and method recovery were important for the calculations, and mass-per-day measurements were normalized by population estimates. Municipal WWTP estimates were used for wastewater and prescription data normalization, while informal settlement population estimates were less certain. Mass loads and normalized loads indicated higher relative usage in settlements for several compounds, and UWF data triangulation with prescription datasets showed good correlations for some antimicrobials while revealing discrepancies for others. The paper concludes that WBE/UWF can provide a comprehensive epidemiological tool for tracking pharmaceutical usage where prescription records are incomplete.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(408,'消费类','咖啡因','咖啡因及代谢物','咖啡因','含咖啡因食品、饮料和相关产品摄入','其他','1,7-二甲基尿酸','33868-03-0','1,7-二甲基尿酸分子量196.06；咖啡因分子量194.08（正文3.2校正因子公式）',14.800000,6.7000,190.0000,'mg/day/person',NULL,NULL,'Caffeine; 1,7-dimethyluric acid; Back-calculation; Correction factor; Wastewater-based epidemiology; Urinary biomarkers','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2017.07.258','Caffeine metabolites in wastewater were investigated as biomarkers for assessing population caffeine intake. The main human urinary metabolites of caffeine were measured in urban wastewater from ten European cities and wastewater metabolic profiles were compared with human urinary excretion profiles. 1,7-dimethyluric acid matched well and was selected as a suitable wastewater biomarker for population-level caffeine consumption. A correction factor was developed using human excretion data from pharmacokinetic studies, and daily caffeine intake estimated from wastewater was compared with coffee trade based intake by country. The study found good agreement in some cities and concluded that wastewater analysis can provide useful local information on caffeine use.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(409,'药物类','精神神经类药物','中枢兴奋/拟交感药','哌甲酯','注意缺陷多动障碍等慢性治疗','处方药','利他林酸','19395-41-6',NULL,NULL,73.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1016/j.envint.2024.108524','With increasing numbers of chemicals used in modern society, assessing human and environmental exposure to them is becoming increasingly difficult. Recent advances in wastewater-based epidemiology enable valuable insights into public exposure to data-poor compounds. However, measuring all > 26,000 chemicals registered under REACH is not just technically unfeasible but would also be incredibly expensive. In this paper, the authors argue that estimating emissions of chemicals based on usage data could offer a more comprehensive, systematic and efficient approach than repeated monitoring. Emissions of 29 active pharmaceutical ingredients to wastewater were estimated for a medium-sized city in the Netherlands. Usage data were collected on national and local scales and included prescription data, usage in health-care institutions and over-the-counter sales. Different routes of administration were considered as well as excretion and in-sewer back-transformation of conjugates. Results suggest model-based emission estimation on a city-level is feasible and in good agreement with wastewater measurements obtained via passive sampling.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(410,'药物类','消炎镇痛药','非甾体抗炎药','双氯芬酸','急性疼痛和炎症治疗','处方药','5-羟基双氯芬酸','6