沙星','100986-85-4',NULL,NULL,85.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1016/j.envint.2024.108524','With increasing numbers of chemicals used in modern society, assessing human and environmental exposure to them is becoming increasingly difficult. Recent advances in wastewater-based epidemiology enable valuable insights into public exposure to data-poor compounds. However, measuring all > 26,000 chemicals registered under REACH is not just technically unfeasible but would also be incredibly expensive. In this paper, the authors argue that estimating emissions of chemicals based on usage data could offer a more comprehensive, systematic and efficient approach than repeated monitoring. Emissions of 29 active pharmaceutical ingredients to wastewater were estimated for a medium-sized city in the Netherlands. Usage data were collected on national and local scales and included prescription data, usage in health-care institutions and over-the-counter sales. Different routes of administration were considered as well as excretion and in-sewer back-transformation of conjugates. Results suggest model-based emission estimation on a city-level is feasible and in good agreement with wastewater measurements obtained via passive sampling.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(414,'药物类','抗生素','磺胺类','磺胺间甲氧嘧啶','抗感染治疗/抗菌药物','处方药','磺胺间甲氧嘧啶','1220-83-3','分子式C11H12N4O3S；分子量280.3；水溶性4030 mg/L；logKow 0.7',NULL,NULL,4.1600,'g/day',NULL,NULL,'Antibiotic; Passive sampling; o-DGT; Wastewater treatment plant (WWTP); China; UK','10.1016/j.envint.2015.10.001','This study used diffusion gradients in thin-films for organics (o-DGT) passive samplers to assess the occurrence and removal of antibiotics in two wastewater treatment plants, one in China and one in the UK. Detected antibiotics in influent and treatment units were quantified, and estimated consumption data were used to interpret differences between catchments and WWTP performance.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(415,'药物类','