nterpret differences between catchments and WWTP performance.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(418,'人群校正类','人群校正标志物','尿液/人口校正标志物','人口校正指标',NULL,'其他','肌酐','60-27-5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chiral drugs; Enantiomers; Chiral chromatography; Wastewater; Wastewater-based epidemiology; Illicit drugs','10.1016/j.chroma.2016.02.015','This paper developed a multi-residue enantioselective CBH-HPLC-MS/MS method for 56 drug biomarkers in wastewater and applied it in a one-week monitoring study at a large UK wastewater treatment plant. The paper includes illicit/abused drug biomarkers and also directly measured population or lifestyle markers including caffeine, 1,7-dimethylxanthine, nicotine, cotinine, and creatinine.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(419,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗癫痫/神经痛用药','卡马西平','癫痫/神经痛','处方药','2-羟基卡马西平','68011-66-5','SI Table 1: MP 236.27 g/mol; MA 252.27 g/mol; DDD 1000 mg',NULL,2.3000,0.7590,'treatments/day/1000 inhabitant',NULL,NULL,'wastewater-based epidemiology; pharmaceuticals; prescription data; measurement-based consumption; Barcelona; Girona','10.1016/j.envint.2021.106404','This study compared wastewater-based measurement consumption estimates for pharmaceuticals with fine spatial-resolution prescription data in Barcelona and Girona, Spain. Influent wastewater from two WWTPs was sampled during 16-20 October 2019 and analysed by LC-MS/MS; supplementary tables report concentrations, back-calculation parameters and MC/PC results.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(420,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗抑郁药','氟西汀','抑郁/焦虑相关治疗','处方药','去甲氟西汀','126924-38-7','SI Table 1: MP 309.33 g/mol; MA 295.3 g/mol; DDD 20 mg',NULL,7.0000,76.0400,'treatments/day/1000 inhabitant',NULL,NULL,'wastewater-based epidemiology; pharmaceuticals; prescription data; measurement-based consumption; Barcelona; Girona','10.1016/j.envint.2021.106404','This study compared wastewater-based measurement consumption estimates for pharmaceuticals with fine spatial-resolution prescription data in Barcelona and Girona, Spain. Influent wastewater from two WWTPs was sampled during 16-20 October 2019 and analysed by LC-MS/MS; supplementary tables report concentrations, back-calculation parameters and MC/PC results.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(421,'药物类','降血脂药','他汀类调脂药','普伐他汀','血脂异常','处方药','普伐他汀','81131-70-6','SI Table 1: MP 424.53 g/mol; MA 424.53 g/mol; DDD 40 mg；SI Table 9: logKow 3.1; logP 2.18; pKa 4.2',NULL,NULL,4.7090,'treatments/day/1000 inhabitant',NULL,NULL,'wastewater-based epidemiology; pharmaceuticals; prescription data; measurement-based consumption; Barcelona; Girona','10.1016/j.envint.2021.106404','This study compared wastewater-based measurement consumption estimates for pharmaceuticals with fine spatial-resolution prescription data in Barcelona and Girona, Spain. Influent wastewater from two WWTPs was sampled during 16-20 October 2019 and analysed by LC-MS/MS; supplementary tables report concentrations, back-calculation parameters and MC/PC results.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(422,'药物类','消炎镇痛药','非甾体抗炎药','安乃近','Pharmaceutical analgesic metabolite of Metamizole/Aminopyrine','处方药','4-乙酰氨基安替比林','83-15-8','SI Table A1: application=Human metabolite (Aminopyrine/Metamizole); molecular weight 245 g/mol; formula C13H15N3O2',1.300000,NULL,1523.0000,'mg/day/1000 inhabitants',NULL,NULL,'Urban wastewater; Urban runoff; Liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry; Online solid-phase extraction; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.envpol.2022.119807','This study developed and applied an online oSPE-LC-MS/MS monitoring setup for high-temporal-resolution analysis of organic micropollutants in WWTP influent and effluent. A simplified WBE approach used daily average influent concentrations from 10-15 December 2020 to estimate measured consumption of selected pharmaceuticals and illicit drugs.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(423,'药物类','降血脂药','调脂药','非诺贝特','血脂异常治疗；用于估计血脂异常患病率','处方药','非诺贝特酸','61002-27-5','非诺贝特主要在肝肾代谢并以非诺贝特酸排泄；中性未处理污水中25°C和4°C降解率<15%，-20°C储存10周降解率<5%',1.490000,66.9500,107.4000,'mg/day/1000 inh',0.0770,54.2000,'Cardiovascular disease; Fenofibrate; Wastewater-based epidemiology; Chronic Disease Prevalence Survey','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.169426','Dyslipidemia, recognized as a predominant risk factor for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (CVD), remains a pressing health concern worldwide, particularly in China with nearly 40% of the population adversely suffering. Fenofibrate, as one of the most commonly used drugs for dyslipidemia therapy, excreted as the format of fenofibrate-acid, showed considerable stability in sewage samples and could be detected as WBE biomarkers to monitor the prevalence of dyslipidemia. In this work, 527 sewage samples from 33 cities in China were extracted by solid phase and analyzed by LC-MS/MS. The detected concentration of fenofibrate acid in sewage was on average 120.5 ± 59.9 ng/L, and the reverse-calculated consumption of fenofibrate based on fenofibrate acid was 77.8 ± 25.0 mg/day/1000inh. The prevalence of fenofibrate was 0.056% ± 0.018%, and the dyslipidemia prevalence among the population aged over 15 was estimated to be 37.9% ± 9.3%.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(424,'药物类','抗生素','磺胺类','磺胺吡啶','抗感染治疗；论文用于抗生素及其人体代谢物的污水监测方法与健康风险评估','处方药','N4-乙酰磺胺吡啶','19077-98-6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'antibiotics; metabolites; simultaneous analysis; stability; wastewater; human health','10.3390/ijerph182010640','The selection and spread of antibiotic resistance poses risks to public health by reducing the therapeutic potential of antibiotics against human pathogens. Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is potentially the most reliable approach to estimate antibiotics use. Previous WBE studies used parent antibiotics as biomarkers, which may lead to overestimation since parent antibiotics may be directly disposed of. Using metabolites as biomarkers can avoid this drawback. This study developed a simultaneous solid-phase extraction coupled with ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry method for analyzing 12 antibiotics and human metabolites in wastewater to help assess health risk. Optimum conditions were achieved using a PEP cartridge at pH 3.0. The extraction efficiencies were 73.3~95.4% in influent and 72.0~102.7% in effluent for most of the target analytes. Method detection limit ranged from 0.1 to 1.5 ng/L for influent wastewater and 0.03 to 0.7 ng/L for effluent wastewater. A stability experiment showed that sulfonamide parents and their metabolites were stable at 4 C, -20 C and -80 C, while macrolides metabolites were more stable than their corresponding parents at 4 C and -20 C. Finally, the method was applied to measure these analytes in wastewater samples collected from three Beijing WWTPs and to derive apparent removal rates. All metabolites were detected in wastewater samples with concentrations ranging from 1.2 to 772.2 ng/L in influent, from <MDL to 235.6 ng/L in effluent. The apparent removal rates of five metabolites were above 72.6%. These results set a solid foundation for applying WBE to evaluate antibiotics use and its public health effects.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(425,'药物类','抗生素','大环内酯类','罗红霉素','抗感染治疗；论文用于抗生素及其人体代谢物的污水监测方法与健康风险评估','处方药','N-去甲基罗红霉素','118267-18-8',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'antibiotics; metabolites; simultaneous analysis; stability; wastewater; human health','10.3390/ijerph182010640','The selection and spread of antibiotic resistance poses risks to public health by reducing the therapeutic potential of antibiotics against human pathogens. Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is potentially the most reliable approach to estimate antibiotics use. Previous WBE studies used parent antibiotics as biomarkers, which may lead to overestimation since parent antibiotics may be directly disposed of. Using metabolites as biomarkers can avoid this drawback. This study developed a simultaneous solid-phase extraction coupled with ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry method for analyzing 12 antibiotics and human metabolites in wastewater to help assess health risk. Optimum conditions were achieved using a PEP cartridge at pH 3.0. The extraction efficiencies were 73.3~95.4% in influent and 72.0~102.7% in effluent for most of the target analytes. Method detection limit ranged from 0.1 to 1.5 ng/L for influent wastewater and 0.03 to 0.7 ng/L for effluent wastewater. A stability experiment showed that sulfonamide parents and their metabolites were stable at 4 C, -20 C and -80 C, while macrolides metabolites were more stable than their corresponding parents at 4 C and -20 C. Finally, the method was applied to measure these analytes in wastewater samples collected from three Beijing WWTPs and to derive apparent removal rates. All metabolites were detected in wastewater samples with concentrations ranging from 1.2 to 772.2 ng/L in influent, from <MDL to 235.6 ng/L in effluent. The apparent removal rates of five metabolites were above 72.6%. These results set a solid foundation for applying WBE to evaluate antibiotics use and its public health effects.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(426,'药物类','抗生素','大环内酯类','阿奇霉素','抗感染治疗；论文用于抗生素及其人体代谢物的污水监测方法与健康风险评估','处方药','去克拉定糖阿奇霉素','117693-41-1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'antibiotics; metabolites; simultaneous analysis; stability; wastewater; human health','10.3390/ijerph182010640','The selection and spread of antibiotic resistance poses risks to public health by reducing the therapeutic potential of antibiotics against human pathogens. Wastewater-based epidemiology (WBE) is potentially the most reliable approach to estimate antibiotics use. Previous WBE studies used parent antibiotics as biomarkers, which may lead to overestimation since parent antibiotics may be directly disposed of. Using metabolites as biomarkers can avoid this drawback. This study developed a simultaneous solid-phase extraction coupled with ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry method for analyzing 12 antibiotics and human metabolites in wastewater to help assess health risk. Optimum conditions were achieved using a PEP cartridge at pH 3.0. The extraction efficiencies were 73.3~95.4% in influent and 72.0~102.7% in effluent for most of the target analytes. Method detection limit ranged from 0.1 to 1.5 ng/L for influent wastewater and 0.03 to 0.7 ng/L for effluent wastewater. A stability experiment showed that sulfonamide parents and their metabolites were stable at 4 C, -20 C and -80 C, while macrolides metabolites were more stable than their corresponding parents at 4 C and -20 C. Finally, the method was applied to measure these analytes in wastewater samples collected from three Beijing WWTPs and to derive apparent removal rates. All metabolites were detected in wastewater samples with concentrations ranging from 1.2 to 772.2 ng/L in influent, from <MDL to 235.6 ng/L in effluent. The apparent removal rates of five metabolites were above 72.6%. These results set a solid foundation for applying WBE to evaluate antibiotics use and its public health effects.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(427,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗抑郁药','舍曲林','论文归类为antidepressants and metabolites','处方药','去甲舍曲林','87857-41-8',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pharmaceuticals; disposal; WBE; wastewater-based epidemiology; at-source wastewater treatment','10.1021/acs.est.1c01274','Down-the-drain disposal of pharmaceuticals remains an overlooked and unrecognized source of environmental contamination that requires nontechnological at-source solutions. Monitoring of 31 pharmaceuticals over 7 days in five wastewater treatment plants serving five cities in South-West UK revealed down-the-drain codisposal of several pharmaceuticals. Direct disposal affected wastewater treatment removal and pharmaceutical loads reaching the receiving environment. The study highlights the need for actions to reduce down-the-drain disposal of unused pharmaceuticals.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(428,'药物类','抗肿瘤/免疫调节药','抗代谢类抗肿瘤药','卡培他滨','论文归类为anticancer','处方药','卡培他滨','154361-50-9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pharmaceuticals; disposal; WBE; wastewater-based epidemiology; at-source wastewater treatment','10.1021/acs.est.1c01274','Down-the-drain disposal of pharmaceuticals remains an overlooked and unrecognized source of environmental contamination that requires nontechnological at-source solutions. Monitoring of 31 pharmaceuticals over 7 days in five wastewater treatment plants serving five cities in South-West UK revealed down-the-drain codisposal of several pharmaceuticals. Direct disposal affected wastewater treatment removal and pharmaceutical loads reaching the receiving environment. The study highlights the need for actions to reduce down-the-drain disposal of unused pharmaceuticals.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(429,'消费类','烟草','尼古丁及代谢物','尼古丁','烟草/尼古丁使用监测；anabasine/anatabine用于降低NRT和电子烟对传统烟草估算的干扰','其他','Anatabine','2743-90-0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Direct injection; Nicotine biomarkers; Anabasine; Anatabine; Nicotine; Wastewater-based epidemiology','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.140551','Wastewater-based epidemiology has been used to estimate tobacco use, but nicotine replacement therapies and e-cigarettes can contribute nicotine metabolites to wastewater. This study developed an enhanced direct-injection LC-MS/MS method for anabasine, anatabine, nicotine, cotinine and hydroxycotinine, evaluated in-sewer stability, and applied the method to 42 daily influent wastewater samples from an Australian WWTP covering approximately 100,000 inhabitants.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(430,'药物类','激素替代品/激素类药物','糖皮质激素/COVID-19 重症治疗相关药物','Dexamethasone','COVID-19 重症或机械通气患者抗炎治疗；主文也说明其可作抗炎/免疫抑制药','处方药','Dexamethasone','50-02-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1002/jeq2.20398','During the COVID-19 pandemic, wastewater surveillance was leveraged as a powerful tool for monitoring community-scale health. Further, the well-known persistence of some pharmaceuticals through wastewater treatment plants spurred concerns that increased usage of pharmaceuticals during the pandemic would increase the concentrations in wastewater treatment plant effluent. We collected weekly influent and effluent samples from May 2020 through May 2021 from two wastewater treatment plants in central Pennsylvania, the Penn State Water Reclamation Facility and the University Area Joint Authority, that provide effluent for beneficial reuse, including for irrigation. Samples were analyzed for severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (influent only), two over-the-counter medicines (acetaminophen and naproxen), five antibiotics (ampicillin, doxycycline, ofloxacin, sulfamethoxazole, and trimethoprim), two therapeutic agents (remdesivir and dexamethasone), and hydroxychloroquine. Although there were no correlations between pharmaceutical and virus concentration, remdesivir detection occurred when the number of hospitalized patients with COVID-19 increased, and dexamethasone detection co-occurred with the presence of patients with COVID-19 on ventilators. Additionally, Penn State decision-making regarding instruction modes explained the temporal variation of influent pharmaceutical concentrations, with detection occurring primarily when students were on campus. Risk quotients calculated for pharmaceuticals with known effective and lethal concentrations at which 50% of a population is affected for fish, daphnia, and algae were generally low in the effluent; however, some acute risks from sulfamethoxazole were high when students returned to campus. Remdesivir and dexamethasone persisted through the wastewater treatment plants, thereby introducing novel pharmaceuticals directly to soils and surface water. These results highlight connections between human health and water quality and further demonstrate the broad utility of wastewater surveillance.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(431,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','β受体阻滞剂','Nadolol','高血压、心绞痛、心律失常、心肌梗死等心血管疾病；源文称 β-blockers 为广泛处方心血管药物','处方药','Nadolol','42200-33-9','分子式 C17H27NO4；分子量 309.4；logKow 0.81；pKa 9.67',1.200000,83.0000,0.9000,'mg/day/1000 inh',NULL,NULL,'Wastewater surveillance; Diffusive gradients in thin-films (DGT); β-blocker drugs; Molecularly imprinted polymer (MIP); Wastewater monitoring','10.1016/j.jhazmat.2024.135753','Wastewater surveillance is an effective and objective approach to monitor contaminant releases and drug usage in the catchment, the estimation requires accurate measurement. In this study, a novel diffusive gradients in thin-film (DGT) technique based on molecularly imprinted polymers (MIPs) for selective measurement of a class of widely prescribed cardiovascular drugs (β-blockers) in wastewater was developed. The synthesized MIPs showed strong affinity and selectivity for the target compounds. The MIP-DGT had large effective capacities, its performance was independent of a wide range of environmental conditions, including pH, ionic strength and dissolved organic matter. Biofouling had little effect on the uptake of target compounds within 7 days. MIP-DGT devices were applied in a Chinese urban WWTP alongside an auto-sampler. Metoprolol concentrations detected were much higher than other β-blockers. Concentrations obtained using MIP-DGT were comparable to the 24 h composite samples using an autosampler. The estimated daily consumption calculated based on the data obtained with MIP-DGT implied that metoprolol and propranolol were the most popular β-blockers in the studied area.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(432,'药物类','精神神经类药物','中枢兴奋/拟交感药','伪麻黄碱','减充血药；感冒和过敏用药','非处方药','1S,2S(+)-伪麻黄碱','345-78-8','分子式 C10H15NO·HCl（Table 1 标准品）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sewage epidemiology; Chiral; Drugs of abuse; Enantiomeric profiling; Wastewater analysis; Amphetamines','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2012.02.019','This paper explores possibilities of applying enantiomeric profiling to solving problems related to estimation of drugs usage in communities via the sewage epidemiology approach: for the identification of whether drug residue results from consumption of illicit drug or metabolism of other drugs, verification of potency of used drugs and monitoring of changing patterns of drugs abuse. Due to the very complex nature of wastewater used in sewage epidemiology, which comes from the whole community rather than one individual, verification of the above is challenging but vital in accurate estimations of drugs abuse as well as providing comprehensive information regarding drug abuse trends. The results of this study indicated that amphetamine in raw wastewater was enriched with R(-)-enantiomer due to its abuse as racemate. Methamphetamine was found to be racemic or to be enriched with S(+)-enantiomer. MDMA was enriched with R(-)-MDMA, which was to be expected as MDMA is abused as racemate. MDA was enriched with S(+)-enantiomer, which suggests that its presence might be associated with MDMA abuse and not intentional MDA use. Out of the four possible isomers of ephedrine only natural 1R,2S(-)-ephedrine and 1S,2S(+)-pseudoephedrine were detected in raw wastewater and their diastereomeric fractions were found to be season dependent with higher contribution from 1S,2S(+)-pseudoephedrine over winter months and an enrichment with 1R,2S(-)-ephedrine during the spring and summer months. These findings were accompanied by a decrease of cumulative concentration of ephedrines throughout the sampling campaign between February and August. This is a very important finding indicating that non-enantioselective measurement of ephedrine concentrations cannot be a reliable indicator of actual potency of ephedrines used.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(433,'药物类','精神神经类药物','中枢兴奋/拟交感药','麻黄碱','支气管扩张剂，用于治疗与哮喘、支气管炎和肺气肿相关的支气管痉挛；文中也提及兴奋剂滥用属性','处方药','1R,2S(-)-麻黄碱','50-98-6','分子式 C10H15NO·HCl（Table 1 标准品）',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sewage epidemiology; Chiral; Drugs of abuse; Enantiomeric profiling; Wastewater analysis; Amphetamines','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2012.02.019','This paper explores possibilities of applying enantiomeric profiling to solving problems related to estimation of drugs usage in communities via the sewage epidemiology approach: for the identification of whether drug residue results from consumption of illicit drug or metabolism of other drugs, verification of potency of used drugs and monitoring of changing patterns of drugs abuse. Due to the very complex nature of wastewater used in sewage epidemiology, which comes from the whole community rather than one individual, verification of the above is challenging but vital in accurate estimations of drugs abuse as well as providing comprehensive information regarding drug abuse trends. The results of this study indicated that amphetamine in raw wastewater was enriched with R(-)-enantiomer due to its abuse as racemate. Methamphetamine was found to be racemic or to be enriched with S(+)-enantiomer. MDMA was enriched with R(-)-MDMA, which was to be expected as MDMA is abused as racemate. MDA was enriched with S(+)-enantiomer, which suggests that its presence might be associated with MDMA abuse and not intentional MDA use. Out of the four possible isomers of ephedrine only natural 1R,2S(-)-ephedrine and 1S,2S(+)-pseudoephedrine were detected in raw wastewater and their diastereomeric fractions were found to be season dependent with higher contribution from 1S,2S(+)-pseudoephedrine over winter months and an enrichment with 1R,2S(-)-ephedrine during the spring and summer months. These findings were accompanied by a decrease of cumulative concentration of ephedrines throughout the sampling campaign between February and August. This is a very important finding indicating that non-enantioselective measurement of ephedrine concentrations cannot be a reliable indicator of actual potency of ephedrines used.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(434,'药物类','其他治疗药物','Licit Drug','甲丙氨酯',NULL,'处方药','甲丙氨酯','57-53-4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'wastewater monitoring; PPCPs; high-risk substances; socioeconomic indicators; demographic indicators','10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.32682','This longitudinal cross-sectional wastewater study analyzed biweekly influent wastewater samples from eight sampling locations across six WWTPs in southern Nevada from May 2022 to April 2023 and compared wastewater drug-use patterns with socioeconomic and demographic indicators.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(435,'药物类','精神神经类药物','抗精神病药','硫必利',NULL,'处方药','硫必利','51012-32-9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Environmental monitoring; Pharmaceutical drugs; UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS; Waste-based epidemiology; Contaminants of emerging concern','10.1016/j.chroma.2023.463896','A UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS screening method for 105 pharmaceutical drugs and metabolites was developed and applied to influent wastewater samples from four anonymous WWTPs in north-western Italy during 2022; Table 2 reports average influent concentrations by site.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(436,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','心血管药物','奈必洛尔',NULL,'处方药','奈必洛尔','118457-14-0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Environmental monitoring; Pharmaceutical drugs; UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS; Waste-based epidemiology; Contaminants of emerging concern','10.1016/j.chroma.2023.463896','A UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS screening method for 105 pharmaceutical drugs and metabolites was developed and applied to influent wastewater samples from four anonymous WWTPs in north-western Italy during 2022; Table 2 reports average influent concentrations by site.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(437,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','心血管药物','普罗帕酮',NULL,'处方药','普罗帕酮','54063-53-5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Environmental monitoring; Pharmaceutical drugs; UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS; Waste-based epidemiology; Contaminants of emerging concern','10.1016/j.chroma.2023.463896','A UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS screening method for 105 pharmaceutical drugs and metabolites was developed and applied to influent wastewater samples from four anonymous WWTPs in north-western Italy during 2022; Table 2 reports average influent concentrations by site.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(438,'药物类','消化系统药物','止吐/胃肠动力药','甲氧氯普胺',NULL,'处方药','甲氧氯普胺','364-62-5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Environmental monitoring; Pharmaceutical drugs; UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS; Waste-based epidemiology; Contaminants of emerging concern','10.1016/j.chroma.2023.463896','A UHPLC-QTOF-HRMS screening method for 105 pharmaceutical drugs and metabolites was developed and applied to influent wastewater samples from four anonymous WWTPs in north-western Italy during 2022; Table 2 reports average influent concentrations by site.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(439,'药物类','抗生素','β-内酰胺类/头孢菌素类','头孢噻肟','抗感染治疗','处方药','头孢噻肟','63527-52-6',NULL,NULL,85.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1371/journal.pone.0108621','The concentration of eleven antibiotics (trimethoprim, oxytetracycline, ciprofloxacin, azithromycin, cefotaxime, doxycycline, sulfamethoxazole, erythromycin, clarithromycin, ofloxacin, norfloxacin), three decongestants (naphazoline, oxymetazoline, xylometazoline) and the antiviral drug oseltamivir\'s active metabolite, oseltamivir carboxylate (OC), were measured weekly at 21 locations within the River Thames catchment in England during the month of November 2009, the autumnal peak of the influenza A[H1N1]pdm09 pandemic. The aim was to quantify the pharmaceutical response to the pandemic and compare this to drug use during the late pandemic (March 2010) and the inter-pandemic periods (May 2011). A large and small wastewater treatment plant (WWTP) were sampled in November 2009 to understand the differential fate of the analytes in the two WWTPs prior to their entry in the receiving river and to estimate drug users using a wastewater epidemiology approach.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(440,'药物类','平喘药/呼吸系统用药','血管收缩减充血药','萘甲唑啉','鼻部减充血','非处方药','萘甲唑啉','835-31-4',NULL,NULL,90.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1371/journal.pone.0108621','The concentration of eleven antibiotics (trimethoprim, oxytetracycline, ciprofloxacin, azithromycin, cefotaxime, doxycycline, sulfamethoxazole, erythromycin, clarithromycin, ofloxacin, norfloxacin), three decongestants (naphazoline, oxymetazoline, xylometazoline) and the antiviral drug oseltamivir\'s active metabolite, oseltamivir carboxylate (OC), were measured weekly at 21 locations within the River Thames catchment in England during the month of November 2009, the autumnal peak of the influenza A[H1N1]pdm09 pandemic. The aim was to quantify the pharmaceutical response to the pandemic and compare this to drug use during the late pandemic (March 2010) and the inter-pandemic periods (May 2011). A large and small wastewater treatment plant (WWTP) were sampled in November 2009 to understand the differential fate of the analytes in the two WWTPs prior to their entry in the receiving river and to estimate drug users using a wastewater epidemiology approach.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(441,'药物类','平喘药/呼吸系统用药','血管收缩减充血药','羟甲唑啉','鼻部减充血','非处方药','羟甲唑啉','1491-59-4',NULL,NULL,35.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1371/journal.pone.0108621','The concentration of eleven antibiotics (trimethoprim, oxytetracycline, ciprofloxacin, azithromycin, cefotaxime, doxycycline, sulfamethoxazole, erythromycin, clarithromycin, ofloxacin, norfloxacin), three decongestants (naphazoline, oxymetazoline, xylometazoline) and the antiviral drug oseltamivir\'s active metabolite, oseltamivir carboxylate (OC), were measured weekly at 21 locations within the River Thames catchment in England during the month of November 2009, the autumnal peak of the influenza A[H1N1]pdm09 pandemic. The aim was to quantify the pharmaceutical response to the pandemic and compare this to drug use during the late pandemic (March 2010) and the inter-pandemic periods (May 2011). A large and small wastewater treatment plant (WWTP) were sampled in November 2009 to understand the differential fate of the analytes in the two WWTPs prior to their entry in the receiving river and to estimate drug users using a wastewater epidemiology approach.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(442,'药物类','降压药/心血管用药','血管紧张素II受体阻滞剂','奥司他韦','流感抗病毒治疗','处方药','奥司他韦羧酸','187227-45-8',NULL,NULL,80.0000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10.1371/journal.pone.0108621','The concentration of eleven antibiotics (trimethoprim, oxytetracycline, ciprofloxacin, azithromycin, cefotaxime, doxycycline, sulfamethoxazole, erythromycin, clarithromycin, ofloxacin, norfloxacin), three decongestants (naphazoline, oxymetazoline, xylometazoline) and the antiviral drug oseltamivir\'s active metabolite, oseltamivir carboxylate (OC), were measured weekly at 21 locations within the River Thames catchment in England during the month of November 2009, the autumnal peak of the influenza A[H1N1]pdm09 pandemic. The aim was to quantify the pharmaceutical response to the pandemic and compare this to drug use during the late pandemic (March 2010) and the inter-pandemic periods (May 2011). A large and small wastewater treatment plant (WWTP) were sampled in November 2009 to understand the differential fate of the analytes in the two WWTPs prior to their entry in the receiving river and to estimate drug users using a wastewater epidemiology approach.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(443,'药物类','消炎镇痛药','非甾体抗炎药','依托考昔','消炎镇痛','处方药','依托考昔','202409-33-4','分子式C18H15ClN2O2S；分子量358.84；水溶解度3.28 mg/L(25°C)；logKow 0.88；pKa 4.5',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Emerging contaminants; Environmental risk; High-resolution mass spectrometry; Greece; Organophosphate flame retardants; Perfluorinated compounds','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2021.149860','Exploring the contamination profile of multi-class emerging contaminants in wastewater is highly desirable. This study investigated occurrence, removal, mass loading and risks for pharmaceuticals and personal care products, illicit drugs, perfluorinated compounds and organophosphate flame retardants in two WWTPs in Thessaloniki, Greece. Influent and effluent wastewaters were extracted by Oasis HLB SPE and analyzed by UHPLC-Orbitrap MS. Caffeine, acetaminophen, irbesartan and valsartan were among the most ubiquitous and elevated compounds, and mass loading plus ecological risk assessment were reported.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(444,'药物类','抗肿瘤/免疫调节药','抗肿瘤药','达卡巴嗪','抗肿瘤治疗','处方药','达卡巴嗪','4342-03-4','分子式C6H10N6O；分子量182.18；水溶解度4220 mg/L(25°C)；logKow -0.24；pKa 4.4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Emerging contaminants; Environmental risk; High-resolution mass spectrometry; Greece; Organophosphate flame retardants; Perfluorinated compounds','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2021.149860','Exploring the contamination profile of multi-class emerging contaminants in wastewater is highly desirable. This study investigated occurrence, removal, mass loading and risks for pharmaceuticals and personal care products, illicit drugs, perfluorinated compounds and organophosphate flame retardants in two WWTPs in Thessaloniki, Greece. Influent and effluent wastewaters were extracted by Oasis HLB SPE and analyzed by UHPLC-Orbitrap MS. Caffeine, acetaminophen, irbesartan and valsartan were among the most ubiquitous and elevated compounds, and mass loading plus ecological risk assessment were reported.','2026-06-15 20:40:21','2026-06-15 20:40:21'),(445,'药物类','抗肿瘤/免疫调节药','抗肿瘤/免疫调节药物','甲氨蝶呤','抗肿瘤治疗','处方药','甲氨蝶呤','59-05-2','分子式C20H22N8O5；分子量454.17；水溶解度2600 mg/L(25°C)；logKow -1.85；pKa 4.7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Emerging contaminants; Environmental risk; High-resolution mass spectrometry; Greece; Organophosphate flame retardants; Perfluorinated compounds','10.1016/j.scitotenv.2021.149860','Exploring